/-!
# Dense-time generation of the continuous-path filtration

At a nonnegative rational terminal time, the canonical filtration on continuous-path space is
already generated by the rational-time coordinates up to that terminal time. This deterministic
fact is the filtration bridge needed to extend finite-cylinder restart identities to all past
events. No probability law or Markov property is asserted here.
-/

open Filter MeasureTheory

namespace MarkovProcess
namespace ContinuousPath

noncomputable section

variable {alpha : Type*} [PseudoMetricSpace alpha]
  [MeasurableSpace alpha] [BorelSpace alpha]













end
end ContinuousPath
end MarkovProcess


